        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Patient admitted with NSTEMI. Underwent cardiac catheterization showing 70% stenosis of LAD. Drug-eluting stent placed successfully. Now requires dual antiplatelet therapy (aspirin + clopidogrel) plus warfarin for AFib = TRIPLE ANTITHROMBOTIC THERAPY. This significantly increases bleeding risk (HAS-BLED score 4). CRITICAL MEDICATION ISSUE: Omeprazole reduces clopidogrel effectiveness by ~50% via CYP2C19 inhibition. SWITCHED omeprazole to pantoprazole 40mg which has minimal interaction with clopidogrel. However, patient still has healing duodenal ulcer, so PPI must continue. Plan for 1 month of triple therapy, then reassess if can discontinue aspirin and continue clopidogrel + warfarin. Close monitoring for bleeding. Hold ferrous sulfate as it can interfere with clopidogrel absorption if taken together.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
